{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# The `supports_temperature` override table is incomplete — the default model is unguarded\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nStory 2932 landed a MEASURED override so Bedrock models that reject `temperature` have it withdrawn rather than hard-failing (`src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py:95`, consumed at `src/rebar/llm/runner.py:399`). The table has exactly ONE entry:\n\n```python\n_MODEL_ID_CAPABILITY_OVERRIDES = {\n    \"us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-7\": {\"supports_temperature\": False},\n}\n```\n\nA fresh measurement sweep shows the behaviour is **family-wide across the opus line and both profile prefixes**, so the single entry leaves rebar's own DEFAULT model unguarded.\n\n## MEASURED — account 896586841071, us-east-1, boto3 `bedrock-runtime.converse`, maxTokens 8\n\n| model id | temp unset | temp=0.0 | temp=0.5 | temp=1.0 | topP=0.9 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` | OK | OK | OK | — | — |\n| `global.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` | OK | OK | — | — | — |\n| `us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8` | OK | **400** | **400** | OK | **400** |\n| `global.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8` | OK | **400** | — | — | — |\n| `us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-7` | OK | **400** | — | — | — |\n| `global.anthropic.claude-opus-4-7` | — | **400** | — | — | — |\n| `us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-5` | ValidationException: invalid model identifier | | | | |\n| `us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5` | ValidationException: invalid model identifier | | | | |\n\nError text: `ValidationException: \\`temperature\\` is deprecated for this model.` (and `\\`top_p\\` is deprecated for this model.`)\n\n## What the data actually says (three corrections to the current model)\n\n1. **`us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8` is affected, and it is rebar's `DEFAULT_MODEL`** (`config.py:39` = `claude-opus-4-8`). The table does not list it, so the guard does not fire. This is the single most likely Bedrock Pass-1 model — especially under the operator requirement that Pass-1 run opus (see eb6e) — and it would hard-fail the moment any temperature is configured.\n2. **The `global.` prefix is affected too.** The table keys on the full model id, so `global.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8` and `global.anthropic.claude-opus-4-7` are both unguarded even if the `us.` twins are listed. Any fix keyed literally per-id must cover both prefixes, or be matched on the family portion.\n3. **It is NOT 'temperature unsupported' — it is 'explicit non-default sampling rejected'.** `temp=1.0` (the API default) SUCCEEDS on opus-4-8 while 0.0 and 0.5 fail. So the deprecation is of the parameter's *tunability*. `supports_temperature=False` still produces correct behaviour (withdraw the parameter → the model uses its default), but the field NAME misdescribes the mechanism, which matters for the next person extending it.\n\n**`top_p` is deprecated on opus-4-8 as well, and there is no `supports_top_p` on the capability record.** This is currently LATENT, not live: rebar never sets `top_p` anywhere in `src/rebar`. But `failure.py:367` already lists `top_p`/`top_k` as sampling parameters rebar 'can send', so the gap becomes live the day anything sets one.\n\n## Why this matters now\n\n- The Pass-2 verifiers deliberately pin `temperature=0` (`code-review.yaml:155`). That is safe ONLY while Pass-2 stays on sonnet, which accepts it. It is the per-pass model split (eb6e) that keeps this from being an outage.\n- The production cutover ships with **no fallback**, so an unguarded 400 here is a stuck gate, not a degraded one.\n- `us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-5` and `us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5` are NOT invokable in this account at all — worth noting because an earlier note in this epic recorded cache measurements for opus-4-5, and that model id does not resolve here now. Any conclusion resting on it should be re-measured rather than trusted.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py` — extend the override table (or match on the family portion of the id so both `us.` and `global.` prefixes are covered by one entry).\n- `tests/unit/` — a test per newly-covered id asserting the parameter is withdrawn.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] a test asserts `capabilities_for(\"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8\").supports_temperature`\n      is False. NOTE the PROVIDER-QUALIFIED form: `_model_id_of` returns None for a bare id with no\n      colon, so a bare-string assertion passes VACUOUSLY against the conservative record without ever\n      exercising the override table. Production always passes `provider:model` or a model object.\n- [ ] a test asserts the same for `global.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8` and for both `opus-4-7` prefixes\n- [ ] a test asserts `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` retains `supports_temperature is True` (the guard must not over-apply and silently drop determinism from the model that supports it)\n- [ ] the table's comment records the measured matrix above, including that temp=1.0 succeeds, so the next reader does not re-derive it"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785460259341623001,"uuid":"f912194d-26c3-4eb5-aae2-9bab0e9fe132"}